DESCRIPTION:$25 General Admission Doors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10:30
 pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$5 off each ticket when you use
  the code earlybird3 at checkout.\n\nOffer ends July 19th.\n\nPromo Codes
  are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitive\, but m
 ust be typed as one word.\n\nSinger-songwriter-guitarist Doug Jayne is c
 o-owner of The Next Record Store in Santa Rosa\, CA\, and hosts Midday Mus
 ic on Sonoma County's NPR affiliate\,KRCB FM. Founder of Jackalope Records
 \, an indie label and recording studio\, Doug has produced dozens of North
 ern California bands and musicians since 1996. Over the years\, Doug has f
 ronted the mildly popular bands\, Stupid White People\, Loser Friendly\, L
 aughing Gravy\, and ClusterFolk.  Doug currently plays with his long-time
  collaborator\, Kevin Russell\, as Jayne-Russell\, doing mostly his origin
 al songs\, and some cool covers.\n\nhttps://www.reverbnation.com/dougjayne
  \n\nKevin Russell is a multi-instrumentalist\, singer and songwriter. H
 e performs regularly in a number of Sonoma county’s most popular bands. 
 All of these groups perform at local club venues\, county fairs\, parties\
 , festivals\, weddings and special events. For nine years Kevin was the dr
 iving force behind The Sebastopol Guitar Festival and currently is the org
 anizer of the Sonoma County Americana Music Festival held in early October
 . In addition to being a musician\, Kevin hosts shows featuring touring mu
 sicians like Joe Craven\, Gonzalo Bergara\, Jim Hurst\, David Lindley\, Ra
 dney Foster\, Jack Tempchin\, Ray Bierl\, Mike Dowling\, Laurie Lewis\, Ka
 thy Kallick\, Missy Raines\, Maria Muldaur & others.\n\nSee thefamiliarst
 rangersmusic.com for more info.
