BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dumpling Workshop with Lani Chan at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T130000
UID:260717wKF6eOuvL064Thb5p8yMkg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a 3-hour hands-on dumpling workshop led by Lani Ch
 an\, founder of Hei Ma\, where you'll learn to make dumplings entirely fro
 m scratch — wrappers\, fillings\, and all. You'll start by making the do
 ugh. From there\, you'll form and cook vegetarian dumplings\, learn to mak
 e scallion pancakes\, and pair everything with Hei Ma chili crisp and a sp
 ecial dipping sauce made with Gold Ridge Organic Farms Apple Cider Balsami
 c Vinegar.\n\nThe experience begins with a scenic ride aboard our apple-th
 emed trolley to the Apple Cottage\, where the class takes place. You'll cr
 eate delicious dumplings to take home and share with friends and family\, 
 and receive a keepsake apple-blossom pink apron. During the class\, you'll
  taste freshly made dumplings accompanied by a refreshing citrus shrub. We
  recommend bringing a cooler in your car to keep your dumplings fresh on t
 he ride home.\n\nWhether you're a seasoned home cook or making dumplings f
 or the first time\, this is an experience you won't forget—good food\, g
 reat company\, and a deeper connection to the ingredients grown right here
  in Sonoma County.\n\nLani Chan is the co-founder of Hei Ma (formerly know
 n as Big Spoon Sauce Co.)\, a Sonoma County-based small-batch sauce brand 
 rooted in Chinese culinary tradition and peak-season California produce. W
 hat began as a chili crisp project in a Brooklyn apartment in 2019 has gro
 wn into a community-driven food brand celebrated for its bold flavors and 
 cultural heart.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/gold-ridge-organic-farms/event/610522/dump
 ling-making-workshop-with-lani-chan
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
