DESCRIPTION:**SIRENS FEST BELLYDANCE FESTIVAL** July 24–26\, 2026 • Se
 bastopol Subud Hall\, 234 Hutchins Ave.\, Sebastopol\n\nSirens Fest return
 s for three days of music\, dance\, culture\, and community. Friday featur
 es workshops in Oriental Bellydance\, Fusion\, Folkloric\, Dumbek\, Burles
 que\, and more. Saturday and Sunday offer nonstop performances\, live Egyp
 tian\, Turkish\, Kurdish\, Lebanese\, and Arabic music\, vendors\, Middle 
 Eastern food\, a full bar\, and a free Shisha tent (21+). Highlights inclu
 de Sirens After Dark Fire Show on Saturday and the Bellydancer of the Univ
 erse Regional Competition on Sunday. Festival hours vary by day. Admission
 : Saturday $30\, Sunday $25. For tickets and information visit www.sirens
 bellydancefest.com.
LOCATION:Sirens Studio at Subud Hall
URL:https://www.facebook.com/sirensfest
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Talks - From Mayberry to Beverly Healdsburg
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T113000
UID:2607149iUOTLDtH0enolzAenpaFw
DESCRIPTION:RUDAT Report & Downtown Before and After\n\nJerry Haag and Joa
 nne Taeuffer\n\nJust 50 years ago\, Healdsburg was seen as a cow town\, bu
 t an urban planning process in 1982 started the change that led to today
 ’s upscale version of the town. Jerry Haag\, a retired city planner\, wi
 ll review the process that was guided by the Regional/Urban Design Assista
 nce Team \\(RUDAT\\) leading Healdsburg to becoming a premier destination 
 for wine country tourism.\n\nJoanne Taeuffer will show how this new vision
  changed the look and feel of the Plaza area from her 1960s “Mayberry”
  version to what she calls “Beverly Healdsburg.”
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
