BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LOBSTER BOIL DINNER plus Spike Sikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T200000
UID:260709THxxtfjUaES4wDO2BTjghw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for one of summer’s most delicious evenings at FOPPI
 ANO VINEYARDS. Beneath the garden pergola at our historic barn\, surrounde
 d by vineyards and sweeping sunset views\, settle in for an unforgettable 
 experience. Enjoy exceptional wine\, live music\, and a memorable lobster 
 boil dinner set to the adventurous sounds of SPIKE SIKES AND HIS AWESOME H
 OTCAKES.\n\nThe evening begins with a wine reception and seasonal bites be
 fore guests gather for an al fresco dinner. CHEF JOSH brings an elevated 
 take on the classic East Coast lobster boil\, served family-style with fre
 sh coastal flavors and seasonal touches\, followed by a sweet finish to en
 d the evening.\n\nThoughtfully paired FOPPIANO wines will flow throughout 
 the night\, creating a warm\, festive gathering that captures the best of 
 summer in Healdsburg—great wine\, generous hospitality\, and the simple 
 pleasure of sharing an unforgettable evening with friends.\n\nJuly 25\, 20
 26 | 5:00 – 8:00 PM $120 Members $150 Public\n\nABOUT SPIKE SIKES AND HI
 S AWESOME HOTCAKES:\n\n“No one is making this kind of music anymore! But
  what\, exactly\, is “this kind of music?”\n\nLike hotcakes themselves
 \, it goes by many names. Soul. Swing. Rhythm & Blues. Jazz. Jump. It’s 
 a sound that’s classic and simple\, but when it’s done right\, it hits
  the spot\, and has you grinning from ear to ear. Spike has spent years se
 arching for this sound.From the Texas blues joints he cut his teeth in to 
 the funky halls of New Orleans\, he was always studying the music\, trying
  to find just the right recipe. It makes perfect sense that he found his b
 andmates in Sonoma County\, a music scene that has fostered many eclectic 
 artists for decades.What he didn’t know was how hungry audiences were fo
 r “this kind of music.” You might say they’ve been eating it up like
 …Hotcakes!
LOCATION:Foppiano Vineyards
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/foppianovineyards/event/602121/lobster-boi
 l-2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plein Air Watercolor Landscapes at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T140000
UID:260709J8GpSAy_f0abuiBPM9QHOQ
DESCRIPTION:Presented in partnership with the Sonoma Community Center\, pa
 rticipants will explore both watercolor technique and the core principles 
 of landscape painting\, including composition\, color temperature\, and at
 mospheric perspective. The group will learn to create movement and depth i
 n a painting and gain a new appreciation for the beauty of the surrounding
 s through the process of close observation and careful rendering.\n\nThe c
 lass begins with quick thumbnail sketches\, then each person selects one c
 omposition to focus on throughout the day. Through demonstration and indiv
 idual instruction\, they learn color mixing and watercolor techniques whil
 e building their painting step by step.  All levels of experience are wel
 come.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/plein-air-watercolor-landscapes-july
 -2026-copy/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JAD Experience presents LUNAE
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T220000
UID:26070911j9IQOOKUeFbR3HweWc9g
DESCRIPTION:JAD Experience\, the trailblazing series uniting regenerative 
 cuisine and world-class ballet\, announces LUNAE\, its milestone 13th seas
 on. Taking place July 17–19 and July 24–26\, LUNAE is an immersive eve
 ning of farm-to-table dining\, world-class ballet under the stars\, and de
 ep connection with nature.\n\nInspired by the 13 lunar cycles of the year\
 , LUNAE’s choreography evokes the timeless rhythms of creation\, surrend
 er\, and renewal through themes of feminine energy\, light\, and shadow.\n
 \nPerched atop Tara Firma Farms \\(3796 I Street Ext.\, Petaluma\, CA 9495
 2\\) with sweeping pastoral views\, LLUNAE delivers on the original social
  ritual: shared culinary experience at long tables. Following dinner\, an 
 intimate ballet performance unfolds beneath the night sky for just 100 gue
 sts each evening.\n\nEvenings begin with arrival and cocktails from 5:30 t
 o 7 p.m.\, followed by dinner from 7 to 8:30 p.m. The experience continues
  with the ballet performance from 8:45 to 9:30 p.m.\, and the evening conc
 ludes at 10 p.m.\n\nFree parking is available\, and all seating offers exc
 ellent views of the open-air stage. Because evenings in Petaluma can cool 
 quickly\, guests are encouraged to bring warm layers\; blankets and hot ch
 ocolate will also be provided. Guests needing assistance may choose betwee
 n a hayride or a shuttle for accessibility.\n\nRenowned choreographer Juli
 a Adam\, an Ottawa native and former San Francisco Ballet principal dancer
  \\(1988–2002\\)\, has created more than 100 works for companies includi
 ng Houston Ballet and the National Ballet of Canada.\n\nFeatured dancers i
 nclude David O’matz \\(Pittsburgh Ballet Theatre\\)\, Augi Lehner\, Ryan
  Williams\, Saela Rivera-Martinez\, Zoe Lucich \\(Bay Area\, Houston Balle
 t\\)\, Harry Warshaw \\(Ballet Memphis\\)\, Lily Mangiaruga \\(New Orleans
  Ballet Theatre\\)\, Kelsey Mcfalls \\(freelance\, Bay Area\\)\, and Tessa
  Barbour \\(Smuin Ballet\, Bay Area\\).\n\nDinner is led by chefs Brian Le
 itner and Annette Yang of Pearl\, presenting a multi-course menu rooted in
  the farm and its surrounding network. The evening features dishes such as
  beef tartare\, summer succotash\, grilled strip loin\, and seasonal desse
 rts\, alongside substantial vegetarian and vegan offerings.\n\nIngredients
  are sourced transparently from Tara Firma Farms and regional partners\, i
 ncluding Umbel Roots\, Feed Sonoma\, True Grass Farms\, and Holistic Ag. B
 everage pairings include wines from Enkidu and Shokrian\, beers from HenHo
 use and Moonlight Brewing\, and house-made nonalcoholic options.\n\nTara F
 irma Farms\, a working cattle ranch stewarded by JAD co-founder Aaron Luci
 ch\, powers this chef-farmer artistry.\n\nIn an era shaped by screen addic
 tion and fleeting digital distractions\, LUNAE offers a return to genuine 
 human connection through live performance\, communal dining\, and an extra
 ordinary natural setting.\n\n“LUNAE follows thirteen lunar cycles\, with
  each phase shaping the timing and movement of the choreography\,” said 
 Julia Adam\, Co-Founder & Choreographer. “The work draws on feminine ene
 rgy\, expressed through exquisite motion\, repetition\, and release.” \
 n\n“We need to become conscious that we are just a part of the natural s
 ystem\,” said Aaron Lucich\, Co-Founder & Tara Firma Farms Managing Part
 ner. “Land and people heal together. LUNAE's farm-driven feasts at long 
 communal tables\, grown from our regenerative soils\, model this: dining a
 s unity\, ballet as connection\, all under the moon to remind us we're a p
 art of nature's own cycles.”
LOCATION:Tara Firma Farms
URL:https://jadexperience.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
