SUMMARY:Valley of the Moon Music Festival Concert 6: American Roots
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T160000
UID:260606hAUwjCiUn0KhrAYdms4PJA
DESCRIPTION:Travel to the 19th-century United States through a program roo
 ted in African American spirituals and American folk traditions. Featuring
  works by Dvořák alongside composers including Harry T. Burleigh\, Flore
 nce Price\, and Charles Ives\, this concert explores the cultural forces t
 hat shaped a distinctly American musical identity.  Arrive early for a fr
 ee pre-concert lecture led by Michael Beckerman. Concert duration: approxi
 mately 2 hours with intermission.\n\nThe Valley of the Moon Music Festival
  returns July 11–26\, 2026\, with Postcards from Dvořák\, a season ins
 pired by the travels\, influences\, and cultural connections behind the co
 mposer’s music. Set in the heart of Sonoma Valley\, the festival brings 
 together internationally acclaimed musicians for historically informed per
 formances that blend world-class classical music with the beauty and charm
  of wine country.
LOCATION:Hanna Center Auditorium
URL:https://valleyofthemoonmusicfestival.org/event/american-roots/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
