BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Conversation Between Arthur Drooker and Richard Neill
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T133000
UID:260722sVG_KVPvVk-F16-XjrTPAA
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a conversation between Photographer Arthur 
 Drooker and Curator Richard Neill about the inspiration for Arthur's photo
 graphic project\, &ldquo\;Thirty-Six Views of the Golden Gate Bridge.&rdqu
 o\;  The conversation between Drooker and Neill includes the process of cr
 eating the exhibit and book and the historical research that went into mak
 ing the photographs. This will be followed by an audience Q&amp\;A. Books 
 will be available for signing at the event.   Richard Neill is a Photograp
 her\, Filmmaker and Curator and a member of the PAC Exhibitions Committee.
  \n\n \n\nPlease note that photography and video recording may take place 
 during this event. By participating\, you grant the Petaluma Arts Center p
 ermission to use your image for storytelling\, marketing\, and/or document
 ation purposes. By registering for this event\, you also agree to receive 
 occasional email communications from Petaluma Arts Center. You may unsubsc
 ribe at any time. Please reach out to info@petalumaartscenter.org with any
  questions.
LOCATION:Petaluma Arts Center
URL:https://mynorthbaytickets.ticketsauce.com/e/a-conversation-between-art
 hur-drooker-and-richard?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T000000
UID:2606064Io1nyaV4EC87g1lvBcHVA
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market is a year-rou
 nd Saturday tradition in Sonoma County\, bringing together local farmers\,
  ranchers\, food artisans\, and neighbors from 8:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. This is
  not just a place to shop\, it's a place to connect directly with the peop
 le who grow your food. As a Slow Food Sonoma County award recipient\, the 
 market prioritizes integrity\, seasonality\, and true farm-to-community re
 lationships. Expect peak-season produce harvested just hours before market
 \, pasture-raised meats\, fresh flowers\, artisan breads\, handcrafted goo
 ds\, and thoughtfully prepared foods that reflect the region's agricultura
 l richness. Visitors can stroll the vibrant open-air market\, sample local
  flavors\, and experience Sonoma County's food culture in its most authent
 ic form. Families\, chefs\, and weekend explorers alike gather here to dis
 cover what's growing now and to support small farms that keep our local fo
 od system strong. Open every Saturday\, rain or shine\, the Santa Rosa Ori
 ginal Certified Farmers Market is a cornerstone of the community and a mus
 t-visit stop for anyone wanting to taste\, shop\, and experience Sonoma Co
 unty at its freshest.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Greg Lamboy Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T000000
UID:260312M0iBRm_wn06Y-NBIqZkrdw
DESCRIPTION:Greg Lamboy is a Northern California singer-songwriter whose p
 erformances combine lyrical honesty\, melodic craft\, and soulful acoustic
  guitar. Known for his confident yet comforting stage presence\, Greg weav
 es together original songs and reimagined favorites that invite listeners 
 to slow down and connect. His music blends strength and sensitivity\, reve
 aling deep emotion without pretense and reminding audiences why live music
  matters. Greg has released five albums and continues to captivate audienc
 es across the region\, both as a solo artist and as frontman for the Ameri
 cana band Pacific Standard.
LOCATION:Viansa Winery
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107941820?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
