BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:American Red Cross Adult and Pediatric First-Aid/CPR/AED Class (Bl
 ended)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T134500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T161500
UID:260608WJZ8pm8RFk6PXe72aezjzw
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to save a life!\n\nFocusing on recognizing and treat
 ing life-threatening situations in the critical minutes before 911 arrives
 \, we will cover how to handle adult and infant cardiac arrest\, choking\,
  heart attack\, severe bleeding and more!\n\nWe'll be using modern manikin
 s and equipment in a small-group setting\, answering questions along the w
 ay. Your American Red Cross certificate will be valid for 2 years.\n\nThis
  is a blended course: Watch the videos and presentations online at your ow
 n convenience before joining your patient and friendly instructor to pract
 ice your new skills!\n\n(This community class event is held at a branch of
  Sonoma County Library. We thank them for their hospitality. They have req
 uested that we mention that this program is neither sponsored by nor affil
 iated with the Sonoma County Library. Done!)\n\nPlease get in touch with a
 ny questions!
LOCATION:Petaluma Regional Library
URL:https://riverpreparedfirstaid.com/community-classes/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley of the Moon Music Festival Concert 7 - Final Years: Going H
 ome
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T160000
UID:260606szOzgxRnJEy5UQYQ16vIgA
DESCRIPTION:Close the 12th season of Valley of the Moon Music Festival wit
 h an evening celebrating the passionate\, folk-inspired music of Smetana\,
  Janáček\, and Dvořák. This triumphant finale honors the composers who
 se works helped define Czech musical identity. Following the performance\,
  guests are invited to raise a glass at a celebratory reception featuring 
 wines from Idell Family Vineyards. Concert duration: approximately 2 hours
  with intermission.\n\nThe Valley of the Moon Music Festival returns July 
 11–26\, 2026\, with Postcards from Dvořák\, a season inspired by the t
 ravels\, influences\, and cultural connections behind the composer’s mus
 ic. Set in the heart of Sonoma Valley\, the festival brings together inter
 nationally acclaimed musicians for historically informed performances that
  blend world-class classical music with the beauty and charm of wine count
 ry.
LOCATION:Hanna Center Auditorium
URL:https://valleyofthemoonmusicfestival.org/event/final-years-going-home/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
