DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T203000
UID:260720_xtmjyeNjEuNmMbfI76Svw
DESCRIPTION:Please join fellow photography enthusiasts for Irena Miles’ 
 presentation on travel photography.\n\nWhether it’s around the corner or
  around the world\, travel photography is all around you. It’s about mor
 e than just documenting a destination\; it’s about capturing the heartbe
 at\, the flavor\, and the story of a place.\n\nIrena will explore how to t
 rain your eye to identify compositional strengths and capture beautiful st
 ories on your travels—whether you are shooting with a professional camer
 a or the phone in your pocket.\n\nOver 15+ years behind the lens\, Irena
 ’s photography travels have taken her both solo and in group settings ac
 ross the globe. She has had the privilege of capturing the light\, people\
 , and landscapes of Thailand\, Cambodia\, Vietnam\, Turkey\, Portugal\, Uk
 raine\, Mongolia\, Morocco\, Italy\, the Eastern Sierras\, and the America
 n Southwest.\n\nCurrently\, she shoots with Sony mirrorless cameras and us
 es Adobe Lightroom\, Photoshop\, and other plug-ins to bring my creative v
 ision for each image to life. Lately\, my personal work has focused on two
  fascinating concepts:\n\nColor Grading: How adjusting the color palette c
 an completely set the emotional tone and feeling of an image.\n\nVisual We
 ight: Understanding the difference between what we think is the subject of
  a photo and where the colors and lighting are actually pointing the viewe
 r's eye.\n\nWhether you are looking to get more out of your dedicated came
 ra or want to learn how to make your mobile photos truly sing\, this prese
 ntation is designed to inspire you for your next adventure.\n\nNapa Valley
  Photographic Society (NVPS) promotes the art and science of photography\,
  providing education\, image appreciation\, inspiration\, exchange of tech
 nologies. Most months we invite guest speakers to evaluate our images.  G
 uests are welcome to attend.  Check the website for more information http
 ://www.napavalleyphotographicsociety.org.
LOCATION:Napa Senior Center
URL:http://napavalleyphotographicsociety.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ulysses Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T180000
UID:26071771SsjVwK-EOTifEAnS4wEw
DESCRIPTION:Join us Monday evenings throughout July at The Sea Ranch Lodge
  for a community reading and discussion inspired by James Joyce’s Ulysse
 s. Part of the worldwide “Ulysses in 80” reading project\, these gathe
 rings connect local readers with a global community moving through the nov
 el together one day at a time.\n\nThe project is co-led by local resident 
 and writer Mark Sanford Gross alongside Dublin-based Joyce scholar Cliona 
 O’Farrelly of Trinity College Dublin. Local readers may also know Mark t
 hrough his storytelling project\, Write Up the Coast\, which focuses on co
 nversation\, connection\, and shared stories along the Mendocino and Sonom
 a Coast.\n\nDesigned to be welcoming\, conversational\, and open to all le
 vels of familiarity\, the evenings are not academic lectures or formal cla
 sses\, but a chance to gather\, reflect\, question\, laugh\, and share the
  experience of reading a famously complex and rewarding work alongside oth
 ers. First-time readers\, longtime Joyce enthusiasts\, and the simply curi
 ous are all encouraged to attend.\n\nEven if you are not actively reading 
 the book\, you are warmly welcome to join the conversation\, listen in\, a
 nd experience the spirit of the project: discovering how even the most cha
 llenging works of art become more approachable when explored together.\n\n
 More information and daily readings:\n\nulyssesin80.com\n\nQuestions or up
 dates:\n\nreadingulyssesin80@gmail.com
LOCATION:Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/ulysses-book-club/19304
 506/2026-07-27T16
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260727T180000
UID:260715LBmPBJaG4US3oqQpf5Q_kA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\nAUGUST EXHIBIT: PAINT
 ING IN FAUVE\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  July 27 – August 30\, 2026\n\nRECEPTION
 : SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow LaLand and G
 en Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to t
 ake part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by
  a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma wine country a
 rtist\, Willow LaLand presents Painting in Fauve\, a collection of oil and
  acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant beauty through the a
 rtist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realistic landscapes\, these
  works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, tapping into the wild
  Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\, “Mt. Tamalpais
 ” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over its undulating slo
 pes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mountain’s grandeu
 r.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with color as it overloo
 ks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us from palette to palat
 e as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine red wine in “Somme
 lier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\, LaLand notes “
 I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in color\, and give a t
 angible realistic impression within a completely fantastical expression.
 ”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her studies as a young g
 irl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspired by early Ame
 rican realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve dramatic realism
 .  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful response to her 
 themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love both her styles a
 nd have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing between the two
 .  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, and participated 
 in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American Art Collector ma
 gazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: LaLand will host t
 he Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n
 \nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Gen Zorich’s Summertime\, hi
 ghlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth of long\, lazy summer
  days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist and environmental scien
 tist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understanding of the natural w
 orld. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating on pastel pads in “S
 ummer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy days.  These works wou
 ld bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of year.  An award-winn
 ing artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has been a longtime participa
 nt in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet the artist: Zorich wil
 l host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, August 4\, 11am to 6 pm
  and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEALDSBUR
 G\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st
  Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creati
 vity with over 20 galleries participating. This month’s special theme: M
 usic and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306
  Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 1
 1am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
