BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Howl at the Moon Hike at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260729T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260729T230000
UID:260630VoVl9PIZqkmD25drxAp_6Q
DESCRIPTION:This rare midweek evening hike ventures to the summit of Jack 
 London State Historic Park under the rising Buck Moon.\n\nAt the height of
  summer\, July’s Buck Moon is named for the time when deer are growing n
 ew antlers in velvet\, a sign of seasonal strength. At Jack London State H
 istoric Park\, it also echoes “*The Call of the Wild*\,” where Buck is
  the central character—a resilient dog shaped by instinct and endurance.
  Together\, these meanings connect the moon above with the surrounding lan
 dscape.\n\nHikers will set out in the late afternoon light and reach the s
 ummit as the sun sets to watch the Buck Moon rise. The return hike will be
  under moonlight—an entirely different way to experience the trail\, whe
 re the park feels just a little wilder.\n\nThis is a strenuous hike of 8+ 
 miles roundtrip. Participants should be prepared for a steady pace\, limit
 ed stops on the ascent\, and hiking in the dark on the return. A headlamp 
 or flashlight is required for the return hike after dark\, and hiking pole
 s are strongly recommended.\n\nPlease bring plenty of water and a snack or
  bagged meal to enjoy at the summit. Dress in weather-appropriate layers a
 nd wear sturdy hiking shoes. Don’t have a headlamp or trekking poles?  
 Park staff will have a limited number available for checkout on a first-co
 me\, first-served basis.\n\n*Pet dogs (non-service animals) are not permit
 ted on backcountry trails in order to protect wildlife. For more informati
 on about dogs at Jack London State Historic Park\, visit https://jacklondo
 npark.com/policies/.*
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/buck-moon-hike/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Acrylic Painting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260729T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260729T130000
UID:2606087lHRBrmVtk6pPHLGwmwQmQ
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nWednesdays\, June 24 – July 29\, 2026 10:00 AM 
 – 1:00 PM Exceptions: July 8 & August 5\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nExper
 ience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nEvent Categories: Drawing & Painting\, Extende
 d Classes\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$250\n\nM
 aterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$250\n\nJoin our 
 6-week acrylic painting course for beginners. Covers color mixing\, brush 
 techniques\, and composition across landscape and abstract styles.\n\nAbou
 t the Class\n\nThis six-week acrylic painting course is designed for begin
 ners and students with minimal experience. The class focuses on the fundam
 entals of painting\, covering basic techniques and skills\, using a variet
 y of approaches. Students will learn how to handle paint and mix colors\, 
 as well as develop composition while exploring a wide range of subject mat
 ter\, including still life\, portraiture\, abstraction\, and the landscape
 . Group discussions and slide presentations are interspersed throughout th
 e course\, as well as time for one-on-one progress reviews with the instru
 ctor. If you have been considering painting this class will open the door 
 for your exploration. Some basic drawing experience suggested. Repeat stud
 ents welcome. Upon registration the instructor will contact you about supp
 lies needed for the class.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-acrylic-pai
 nting/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
