BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Much Ado About Nothing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T193000
UID:260602dvmkO49A3k2DgVuTpql4lA
DESCRIPTION:**It’s Shakespeare in the Piazza at Bacchus Landing**!\n\nWh
 ile Claudio and Hero fall in love and get engaged\, the villainous Don Joh
 n tricks Claudio into believing Hero is unfaithful\, leading him to public
 ly humiliate her at the altar. Meanwhile\, their friends conspire to make 
 the sparring Beatrice and Benedick fall in love\, and they eventually conf
 ess their feelings for each other. The play’s climax\, in pure Shakespea
 rean form\, involves a faked death\, a confession of Don John’s plot\, a
 nd a happy ending with a double wedding – of course!\n\nBacchus Landing
 ’s wood-fired pizza will be available for purchase\, and wine by the gla
 ss or bottle will also be available for purchase from selected wineries ea
 ch evening (see the schedule\, below). **Sorry\, no outside food or drink
  allowed except for water bottles.** Remember\, Sonoma County evenings ge
 t chilly even in the summer. We advise you to bring a sweater\, jacket\, o
 r hoodie in case you need to bundle up after sunset!\n\nJuly 23rd\, 24th\,
  25th\, 30th\, 31st\; August 1st\, 6th\, 7th. 7:30 pm.\n\nBy William Shake
 speare Directed by Steven David Martin Running time: 2:15 hours Doors open
  at 6:30 pm. **Come early to enjoy Bacchus Landing wood-fired pizza and s
 elect wines!** Free parking is available and the premises are wheelchair-a
 ccessible.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing 
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/much-ado-about-nothing/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pottery on the Wheel\; All Levels with Deborah Donahower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T170000
UID:260602Tv1jTdJz1E2d1Y_558S4MQ
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nThursdays Weekly · 8 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nJune
  11 – July 30\, 2026\n\n2:00 PM – 5:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ce
 ramics Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Lev
 el\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$265\n\nMateria
 ls Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nProgram overview\n\n
 Deborah Donahower takes you through the fundamentals of working with clay 
 in on the wheel in this 8 week course. Designed for all levels \\(beginner
 s and those more experienced\\) Deborah thoughtfully explores the tried an
 d true techniques of ceramic work with her students through structured ass
 ignments\, allowing her students to develop their own creative voice in th
 e process.Students will receive instruction in wheel work\, glazing\, and 
 finishing pieces. With your 8 week class registration\, students receive t
 he opportunity to purchase a studio pass for ½ off during the duration of
  their class. Sign ups for membership will be included in your pre class e
 mail.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/pottery-on-the-wheel-all-le
 vels-with-deborah-donahower/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TAKE YOUR TIME: Oil Pintings by Sharon Eisley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T170000
UID:260529BqFhyJLUbU2cUv0jSRrZag
DESCRIPTION:“Take Your Time”\n\nChange and transformation take time. I
 n her newest oil paintings Sharon Eisley explores the time as a process. B
 e it moving through grief\, re-framing your story of self\, or birthing so
 me new creation\, each painting lures you in with beautiful application th
 en holds you in time for a closer examination of our human experience. Eis
 ley's paintings are all inspired by tarot cards and her personal journey. 
 Tarot readings will be offered at the reception by @SymbolWarehouse for an
  optional small donation.\n\nOur guest artist\, Robert Benson\, will be ch
 allenging your eyes to fill in the details with his impressionist watercol
 ors.\n\nThis June 20th reception will be the FINAL art opening for Sebasto
 pol Gallery in its home of almost 20 years! This show may last only throug
 h June 2026\, then move to our new location. Or it may be up through June 
 and July. Either way\, this will be your last chance to come celebrate our
  local\, amazing group of artists at 150 N Main St.. “Take Your Time” 
 is a reminder to our collective to take our time finding and setting up ou
 r new home for all of you. I hope you can all come celebrate all the time 
 and art we shared with you in our lovely gallery.\n\nwww.sharoneisley.com
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
