BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caesar - Shakespeare in the Park(ing Lot)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T211500
UID:260703wN2vf1YfdUOhy98IQBYqmg
DESCRIPTION:Free Shakespeare in the Park(ing Lot). Elections\, ego\, fear.
  Caesar climbs. The republic fractures.\n\nWe are excited to announce ‘S
 hakespeare in the Park(ing Lot)’ 2026.\n\n***Free Shakespeare.***\n\n**C
 aesar**\n\nPresented by the Jacobethan Theatre Workshop.\n\nDoors open at
  6.75pm\, performance at 7.30pm.\n\nOn Sundays\, doors open at 2.15pm with
  as 3pm start.\n\nDirected by Lukas Raphael\n\n*Caesar* unfolds in 100 mi
 nutes of sharp\, modern storytelling. A political system strains under amb
 ition\, loyalty fractures\, and public rhetoric turns volatile. With minim
 al staging and contemporary dress\, the play lands uncomfortably close to 
 the present: a study of power\, perception\, and how quickly a republic ca
 n shift.\n\nNo intermission.\n\nThe performance will take place in an open
 -air field of the 6th Street Playhouse near the Railroad Square\, Santa Ro
 sa\, CA 95401.\n\nWe will provide limited amount of seating up to 99 seats
  which can be reserved. There is also space to bring lawn chairs\, first-c
 ome-first-seated.\n\n**Please be aware of the cool evenings and we highly 
 recommend to bring a warm jacket.**\n\nA local selection of wine and beer 
 can be purchased in the theater.\n\nLimited parking at 6th Street Playhous
 e and further street-parking is available at Depot Park\, and we recommend
  coming early or looking for parking under the over-pass of Redwood Hwy 10
 1.\n\nIn association with 6th Street Playhouse\, and the Historical Railro
 ad Square Association.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://www.jacobethan.org/parking-lot
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
