UID:260722V0GF178UYE-to7XunO34Eg
DESCRIPTION:STARMAN SF RETURNS TO THE CALIFORNIA THEATRE  ✨ We are beyon
 d thrilled to announce that Starman is returning to the beautiful Californ
 ia Theatre for a special seated\, immersive Bowie experience. This isn’t
  just a concert. It’s a journey. Settle into the historic glow of the th
 eater as we guide you through the eras — from glam to Berlin\, from cosm
 ic spectacle to intimate soul — with stunning musicianship\, theatrical 
 energy\, and a modern\, authentic sound that honors the magic of Bowie. Ex
 pect: ✨ Iconic hits ✨ Deep cuts ✨ An immersive sonic experience This
  is Bowie in a theater the way it was meant to be felt — up close\, inte
 ntional\, and unforgettable. Tickets and details coming soon. Let’s take
  a walk through the stardust together.  ✨
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1564777625653267/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Stray Cats With Special Guest MoonShine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260731T200000
UID:260722LoUFn1EJsEu_jVgEi0wFeA
DESCRIPTION:Back to All Shows\n\nThe Stray Cats\n\nFriday\, July 31\, 2026
 \n\n8:00 pm\n\nBUY TICKETS\n\n🔑 Featuring a pre‑show Club for members
 hip levels $500\\+. Click here for info.\n\n \n\nThe Stray Cats\, the band
  that put Rockabilly music back on the record charts in the early ’80s\,
  scored several big hits on both sides of the Atlantic. All thanks to genu
 ine musical chops that evoke the best players of rockabilly’s original h
 eyday and a striking visual 1950s style made contemporary with exaggerated
  pompadours and colorful tattoos. \n\nThe Stray Cats was formed on Long Is
 land in 1979 by guitarist/vocalist Brian Setzer\, upright bass player Lee 
 Rocker\, and drummer Slim Jim Phantom\, all who shared a love for Rockabil
 ly music. After banging around New York for a few months in the summer of 
 1980\, they saw a kid in a pompadour on the cover of UK magazine NME and h
 opped a plane to London\, where a rockabilly revival movement was just beg
 inning to emerge. Their massive hits and videos include “Runaway Boys\,
 ” “Rock This Town\,” “Stray Cat Strut” “\\(She’s\\) Sexy \\+
  17\,” and “I Won’t Stand in Your Way.” \n\n \n\nTHIRD PARTY RESEL
 LERS\n\nDon’t get taken by deceptive online resellers who use bots to bu
 y tickets and then mark up their prices. The only safe way to protect your
  purchase and guarantee the best seats at the lowest cost is to work direc
 tly with us: through our website\, by phone\, or at our box office in Sant
 a Rosa. Plus\, we’re not bots. Our friendly team members are easily acce
 ssible by phone or at the box office to provide customer support.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/stray-cats26/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
