BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caesar - Shakespeare in the Park(ing Lot)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T164500
UID:260703NvX3iICFDUSqfzdLTE-lEw
DESCRIPTION:Free Shakespeare in the Park(ing Lot). Elections\, ego\, fear.
  Caesar climbs. The republic fractures.\n\nWe are excited to announce ‘S
 hakespeare in the Park(ing Lot)’ 2026.\n\n***Free Shakespeare.***\n\n**C
 aesar**\n\nPresented by the Jacobethan Theatre Workshop.\n\nDoors open at
  6.75pm\, performance at 7.30pm.\n\nOn Sundays\, doors open at 2.15pm with
  as 3pm start.\n\nDirected by Lukas Raphael\n\n*Caesar* unfolds in 100 mi
 nutes of sharp\, modern storytelling. A political system strains under amb
 ition\, loyalty fractures\, and public rhetoric turns volatile. With minim
 al staging and contemporary dress\, the play lands uncomfortably close to 
 the present: a study of power\, perception\, and how quickly a republic ca
 n shift.\n\nNo intermission.\n\nThe performance will take place in an open
 -air field of the 6th Street Playhouse near the Railroad Square\, Santa Ro
 sa\, CA 95401.\n\nWe will provide limited amount of seating up to 99 seats
  which can be reserved. There is also space to bring lawn chairs\, first-c
 ome-first-seated.\n\n**Please be aware of the cool evenings and we highly 
 recommend to bring a warm jacket.**\n\nA local selection of wine and beer 
 can be purchased in the theater.\n\nLimited parking at 6th Street Playhous
 e and further street-parking is available at Depot Park\, and we recommend
  coming early or looking for parking under the over-pass of Redwood Hwy 10
 1.\n\nIn association with 6th Street Playhouse\, and the Historical Railro
 ad Square Association.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://www.jacobethan.org/parking-lot
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live at Juilliard: Michelle Lambert - Pop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T190000
UID:260722WxL4MhiYsk66Yf5ptBwQVA
DESCRIPTION:✨ Experience an unforgettable evening with Michelle Lambert 
 at Live at Juilliard! Join us on Sunday\, August 2\, from 5–7 p.m. in hi
 storic Juilliard Park for a free\, family-friendly concert featuring one o
 f the Bay Area’s most exciting rising artists. Michelle Lambert is a bre
 akout pop singer-songwriter known for her powerful vocals\, captivating so
 ngwriting\, and electrifying stage presence. Michelle has topped the chart
 s on Indie Radio with her original music and was featured in the San Franc
 isco Giants' City Connect Campaign as a standout Bay Area artist. After ho
 ning her craft in the highly competitive music scenes of Nashville and Los
  Angeles\, she has developed a dynamic sound and live show that captivates
  audiences from the very first note. Whether she's delivering soaring pop 
 anthems or heartfelt originals\, Michelle brings energy\, talent\, and aut
 henticity to every performance. Learn more: www.michellelambert.com Enjoy 
 local beer and wine while supporting the Kiwanis Club Santa Rosa  Come hun
 gry! Grab dinner from Costas Tacos and Citas Kitchen  Grab a treat with So
 noma Churros  Bring your lawn chairs\, blankets\, family\, and friends for
  an evening of incredible live music\, delicious food\, and summer fun in 
 the heart of Santa Rosa. The 31st Annual Live at Juilliard Concert Series 
 offers free concerts every Sunday from 5–7 p.m. in Juilliard Park. Learn
  more: www.srcity.org/arts
LOCATION:Juilliard Park
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1036337409070260/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
