BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Estero Trail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T140000
UID:2607225Zslye1y5UCs1lrGrFCRSg
DESCRIPTION:Directions: Meet at the Estero Trailhead. From Hwy 101 in Lark
 spur\, take the exit for Sir Francis Drake Blvd west 20.4 miles to Olema. 
 Turn right onto Hwy 1 and go 2 miles. Follow Sir Francis Drake Blvd 8.4 mi
 . Turn left at the "Estero Trail" sign follow .8 miles to trailhead parkin
 g.\n\nSponsor: Parks\n\nAccommodation Information: If you are a person wit
 h a disability and require an accommodation to participate in a County pro
 gram\, service\, or activity\, requests may be made by calli ng 415-473-43
 81 \\(Voice\\)\, Dial 711 for CA Relay \, or by submitting a\n\nDisability
  Accommodation Request\n\nat least five business days in advance of the ev
 ent. We will do our best to fulfill requests received with less than five 
 business days' notice. Copies of documents are available in alternative fo
 rmats upon request.\n\nThis trail will take us through a variety of habita
 ts offering the opportunity to see songbirds\, raptors\, and ea rly migrat
 ing shorebirds. If we're lucky we might even spy leopard sharks moving thr
 ough the shallow bay waters. Total miles: 4. Elevation change: 150'. This 
 walk is offered in partnership with Point Reye s National Seashore. Rememb
 er to bring lunch\, and binoculars if you have them. No pets are allowed\,
  except for service/companion animals. Adverse weather or poor air quality
  may cancel. Registration is required.\n\nQuestions: Contact\n\nShannon Bu
 rke .
LOCATION:Point Reyes National Seashore
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
