BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T180000
UID:260715BW2Z5KkT4kWcOZ19GchGyg
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\nAUGUST EXHIBIT: PAINT
 ING IN FAUVE\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  July 27 – August 30\, 2026\n\nRECEPTION
 : SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow LaLand and G
 en Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to t
 ake part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by
  a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma wine country a
 rtist\, Willow LaLand presents Painting in Fauve\, a collection of oil and
  acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant beauty through the a
 rtist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realistic landscapes\, these
  works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, tapping into the wild
  Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\, “Mt. Tamalpais
 ” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over its undulating slo
 pes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mountain’s grandeu
 r.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with color as it overloo
 ks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us from palette to palat
 e as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine red wine in “Somme
 lier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\, LaLand notes “
 I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in color\, and give a t
 angible realistic impression within a completely fantastical expression.
 ”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her studies as a young g
 irl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspired by early Ame
 rican realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve dramatic realism
 .  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful response to her 
 themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love both her styles a
 nd have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing between the two
 .  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, and participated 
 in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American Art Collector ma
 gazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: LaLand will host t
 he Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n
 \nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Gen Zorich’s Summertime\, hi
 ghlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth of long\, lazy summer
  days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist and environmental scien
 tist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understanding of the natural w
 orld. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating on pastel pads in “S
 ummer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy days.  These works wou
 ld bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of year.  An award-winn
 ing artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has been a longtime participa
 nt in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet the artist: Zorich wil
 l host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, August 4\, 11am to 6 pm
  and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEALDSBUR
 G\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st
  Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creati
 vity with over 20 galleries participating. This month’s special theme: M
 usic and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306
  Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 1
 1am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T183000
UID:260705fZzXn5oILEaNHGCkGMzMng
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-08-04T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T200000
UID:260704cJCDFE8EZ0eti6OowCHLBg
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 7:00 pm – 8:00 PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-class-intermediate-tuesday/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writers' Showcase
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260804T150000
UID:2606260f-f1c9il0ujC-gRrf52ZA
DESCRIPTION:Long-time Lake County resident Roy Dufrain Jr recently publish
 ed his debut novel\, The Blues and Billie Armstrong\, which is set in the 
 fictional town of Lupoyoma\, based on the city of Lakeport.\n\nDufrain gre
 w up in Lakeport and has lived in Lake County much of his adult life. He g
 raduated from Clear Lake High School\, received his bachelor’s degree fr
 om Sonoma State University\, and is a graduate of the Novel Writing Certif
 icate Program at Stanford University.\n\nPrior to retirement\, Dufrain was
  the owner and operator of HomeMade Publications\, which published local a
 nd regional magazines such as the Mendocino Travelers Guide and Konocti Vi
 sitor. Before that he was the prodution director of the Lake County Record
 -Bee.\n\nHe now resides in Alabama with his wife Jacqueline\, his father R
 oy Sr.\, and a precocious goldendoodle named Andy.\n\nThe Blues and Billie
  Armstrong follows Archer King—first as a thirteen-year-old boy in 1970\
 , grappling with grief\, masculinity\, and the chaotic arrival of his reb
 ellious stepsister Billie\, and then as a prize-winning newspaper columnis
 t renowned as a fearless truth-teller. At the height of his success\, Bill
 ie is captured after decades as a fugitive. Archer can clear her name only
  by revealing the secrets he’s kept hidden for forty years. Secrets that
  will risk his career\, his self respect…and ultimately his freedom.
URL:http://lakearts.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
