SUMMARY:History Talks - Rest in Peace
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T113000
UID:260526Nn-pylW3dkySgzLfuLr-OA
DESCRIPTION:**Death Rituals & The Cemetery’s History**\n\nIn the Victori
 an age\, death was surrounded by strict rituals and rites. Stopped clocks\
 , covered mirrors\, heavy black veils and jewelry woven from the deceased&
 #39\;s hair were all part of the story.\n\nFran Schierenbeck will take you
  on a tour of these rites. And Jim Dreisback will tell the history of Oak 
 Mound\, one of Sonoma County’s oldest cemeteries\, from its establishmen
 t in 1859 through various owners and its renaissance in the last 10 years 
 as the Museum\, local service clubs and businessmen have worked to restore
  the old section and renovate the historic fountain.
LOCATION:Healdsburg Plaza Gazebo
URL:https://www.healdsburgmuseum.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
