BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santa Rosa Taco Tuesday Bike Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T000000
UID:260504td3ZJgcr40yay7wg24gZZg
DESCRIPTION:A fun community bike ride through the heart of Santa Rosa. Com
 e join us this Tuesday! We roll through the JC and McDonald Ave neighborho
 od\, stop in Courthouse Square\, then on to the taco trucks at Mitote Food
  Park in Roseland for dinner! We depart Mitote at 8:15pm\, ride back throu
 gh Courthouse Square\, then on to Yogurt Farms for dessert. This ride is 8
  miles round trip and rides all year long. Rides canceled for rain and hol
 idays. All riders welcome. Bring the whole family! Meet at SRJC parking lo
 t at 550 Silva Ave. We are renting the use of this parking lot every Tuesd
 ay from 5:30pm to 9:30 pm. Taco Tuesday riders can park in the lot during 
 that time frame for free. Please park cars along the back wall on the east
  side. And stage in the row on the northern side of the lot \\(closest to 
 Silva Ave\\). Meet at 5:30pm\; pedals up at 6pm.
LOCATION:SRJC Parking Lot
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roller Disco Daze
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260812T200000
UID:260716N-MvW0BiSkWWDsr1vNlKSQ
DESCRIPTION:Marin Center presents Roller Disco Daze\, a free community rol
 ler skating experience on Lagoon Island at the Marin County Fairgrounds. R
 unning Wednesdays through Sundays\, July 17 through August 16\, the rink i
 s open to all ages and skill levels\, with themed nights every Friday\, Sa
 turday\, and Sunday to keep things lively all summer long. \n\nSkate bene
 ath a disco ball surrounded by the lagoon\, then cool down with lawn games
 \, explore art installations by local artists on display\, and don't miss 
 the giant inflatable skate for the ultimate photo opp. A DJ spins on-site 
 beginning at 12 pm every Friday-Sunday to keep the music on point and the 
 vibes rolling. Food from Manny's Tacos will be on-site all days of the eve
 nt\, and Lobo's Ice Cream will be available July 17-19 and July 24-26.\n\n
 Admission is free. Skate rentals\, including kids' sizes\, are available o
 n-site for $5. All skaters must sign a waiver\; skaters under 18 require a
  parent or guardian signature.
LOCATION:Lagoon Island\, Marin County Fairgrounds
URL:https://marincenter.marincounty.gov/node/306
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
