DESCRIPTION:On Saturday\, August 15 from 5–9 p.m.\, Little Saint\, the 1
 00% plant-based restaurant in Healdsburg\, and Michelin-recognized Italian
  restaurant\, A16\, are coming together for Tomato Sagra: A one-night-only
  plant-based dinner celebrating Southern Italian tradition and California'
 s peak tomato season. \n\nTomato Sagra brings together Chef Deborah Mulli
 n of Little Saint and Chef Valentin Atayde of A16 for a collaborative prix
  fixe dinner inspired by Southern Italy and Sonoma County's peak tomato se
 ason. Together\, the two culinary teams will showcase the season's juicies
 t\, sun-ripened tomatoes across a menu designed to capture the magic of su
 mmer. Imagine dishes like cold-cured olive misti with pickled cherry tomat
 oes\, oven-dried cherry tomatoes on the vine\, A16's signature Naples-styl
 e pizza\, and more — all featuring ingredients sourced from Little Saint
 's eight-acre regenerative farm.
