BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Painting in Fauve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T180000
UID:260715nvS-1CQxJkqTL-BxsKcVnA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  7/15/26\n\nAUGUST EXHIBIT: PAINT
 ING IN FAUVE\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  July 27 – August 30\, 2026\n\nRECEPTION
 : SATURDAY\, August 1\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Willow LaLand and G
 en Zorich\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show.  Be sure to t
 ake part in the Gallery’s free monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by
  a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.\n\nSonoma wine country a
 rtist\, Willow LaLand presents Painting in Fauve\, a collection of oil and
  acrylic paintings focusing on our region’s vibrant beauty through the a
 rtist’s Fauvist lens.  Known for her hyper-realistic landscapes\, these
  works take an imaginative turn to the fantastical\, tapping into the wild
  Fauve vivid color palette.   Highlighting the show\, “Mt. Tamalpais
 ” comes alive\, swathed in rich colors cascading over its undulating slo
 pes\, while rich foreground purple/blues heighten the mountain’s grandeu
 r.  “Fitch Mountain” similarly seems to sing with color as it overloo
 ks a lush vineyard.  LaLand’s color lens takes us from palette to palat
 e as she captures the luxuriant purple/reds of a fine red wine in “Somme
 lier’s Dream.”  Reflecting on her creative process\, LaLand notes “
 I love the artistic freedom to play\, create depth in color\, and give a t
 angible realistic impression within a completely fantastical expression.
 ”\n\nA third-generation artist\, LaLand started her studies as a young g
 irl and had a studio space at 10 years old.  She is inspired by early Ame
 rican realists and uses traditional techniques to achieve dramatic realism
 .  LaLand finds the Fauve color palette elicits a joyful response to her 
 themes of nature and wine.  Many of her collectors love both her styles a
 nd have a hard time\, though they vastly differ\, choosing between the two
 .  LaLand exhibits widely\, including internationally\, and participated 
 in the Art Trails Program.  She was featured in American Art Collector ma
 gazine in 2013 and on KRCB in 2015.\n\nMeet the artist: LaLand will host t
 he Gallery on August 2\, 2:30 – 6pm and August 16 & 29\, 11am to 6 pm.\n
 \nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Gen Zorich’s Summertime\, hi
 ghlighting the beauty of wine country and the warmth of long\, lazy summer
  days.  From Zorich’s background as a geologist and environmental scien
 tist\, she imbues her paintings with a deep understanding of the natural w
 orld. Focusing on flora\, pink waterlilies floating on pastel pads in “S
 ummer Color” engender a sense of sun-filled easy days.  These works wou
 ld bring a feeling of summer contentment any time of year.  An award-winn
 ing artist\, Zorich has exhibited widely and has been a longtime participa
 nt in the Sonoma County Art Trails Program.\n\nMeet the artist: Zorich wil
 l host the Gallery on August 2\, 11am – 2:30pm\, August 4\, 11am to 6 pm
  and August 21 & 23\, 2:30 – 6pm.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEALDSBUR
 G\, Thursday\, August 6\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st
  Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and creati
 vity with over 20 galleries participating. This month’s special theme: M
 usic and Mocktails.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306
  Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 1
 1am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net \n\nFor further informatio
 n: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-
 1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Galler
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poetry that Opens the Dharma Heart to Compassion and Insight
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T163000
UID:260715fWU4AKY1FUiDC_Dlbd5HHg
DESCRIPTION:with Phillip Moffitt\n\nFor 26 years\, Phillip Moffitt has off
 ered this beloved annual gathering—a daylong where poetry reading and pr
 actice interweave to illuminate the Buddha’s path of awakening.\n\nIn th
 is unique daylong\, sitting and walking meditation are woven together with
  the living voice of poetry. Each poem is selected by Phillip to point dir
 ectly at Dharma insights—the truths that free us\, soften us\, and help 
 us see the world through eyes of wisdom and compassion. Part of the joy of
  this day is that participants recite the poetry selections to the group i
 n attendance.\n\nThese are poems that comfort and inspire\, that carry our
  meditation understandings off the cushion and into the lived experience o
 f our daily lives. This is also a day of joy and lightheartedness. If you
 ’ve never read a poem aloud to others\, let this be your invitation to f
 ree your voice and discover a new form of expression.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/poetry-that-opens-the-
 dharma-heart-to-compassion-and-insight-pm1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stand-up + Improv = STANDPROV | Downtown Santa Rosa Good Times
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T210000
UID:260715Y6ayDYy2r0q9_fENJQxsQg
DESCRIPTION:Stand-up + Improv = STANDPROV | Downtown Santa Rosa Good Time\
 n\nThe StandProv cocktail mixes stand-up comedy and improv\, sourced from 
 the best of Northern California comedians and improvisers. StandProv frank
 ensteins together the best parts of standup and improv comedy. Standup com
 edians perform their most time-tested bits\, which then become the inspira
 tion for a cast of improvisers to build out characters\, scenes\, and prem
 ises. Pairing non-stop entertainment with good vibes distills the balanced
  portmanteau commonly referred to in layman's terms as StandProv .\n\nFeat
 uring premier Bay Area comedians and improvisers\, StandProv offers a uniq
 uely familiar performance experience to fans of standup\, improv\, and exp
 erimental art-form fusions alike!\n\nHosted By:  Franco Tevini A talented
  standup comedian and host of StandProv \, Franco performs digestible bits
  of surreal\, elevated slice-of-life comedy.  Jeremy Lessnau A Sonoma cou
 nty based improvisational comedian/musician\, who co-hosts StandProv as eq
 ual parts passion-project and court-ordered community service.\n\nIf you w
 ant to be part of an off-the-wall live anniversary experience—one that i
 s sure to be a memorable night of gut-busting laughter—grab a seat for S
 tandProv at Barrel Proof Lounge in downtown Santa Rosa\, Saturday\, August
  15!\n\nVIP TABLES NOW AVAILABLE! Snag a table for 4 with preferred seatin
 g\, your own private call button to summon service\, and your first round 
 of beer/cider (or a bottle of wine) for only $95!\n\n21+ Doors @6/Show @7 
 $15adv / $20door "Equal parts standup and improvisational comedy\, StandPr
 ov electrifies audiences who enjoy a laugh of any kind"\n\nCheck out **www
 .BarrelProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/stand-up-improv-standprov-downtown-santa-
 rosa-good-times-tickets-1993777284529?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sugarloaf's Trees - From the Oaks to the Redwoods
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T120000
UID:260713J8GkDm2M-UyRmMbvoExt3g
DESCRIPTION:How many kinds of oaks can we find and what makes t
 hem so special? Yes\, Sugarloaf does have Redwoods but why are 
 they so rare? Beginning at the Visitor Center\, we’ll follow P
 ony Gate Trail’s grassy slope\, into the Oak woodland and thro
 ugh a mixed evergreen forest\, along Canyon Trail’s shady ripar
 ian corridor lined with redwoods\, to the 25-foot dramatic plunge
  of Sonoma Creek and back to the Visitor Center. \n\nMeet outsi
 de the Visitor Center. Tickets are $10 for general audiences\, $
 5 for students\, youth\, Sugarloaf members\, Sugarloaf volunteers\,
  and free for children under 12 years old \\(must be accompanie
 d by a parent or legal guardian\\). Tickets on site day of are
  $15 and might not be available. Bring at least a quart of wat
 er\, sun protection\, appropriate footwear for rocky/slippery trail
 s\, and if desired\, a snack.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/sugarloaftrees26
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
