BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Extended Run: Who Will Dance with Pancho Villa?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T193000
UID:2607073HX0I26zSEmputHz1VrGGQ
DESCRIPTION:*Who Will Dance with Pancho Villa?* played to sold-out audien
 ces in January. First performed off-Broadway in 1994\, the playwrights upd
 ated the story with the introduction of the **Ballet Folklórico Legado d
 e Mi Alegría de Cloverdale Ca** while developing the play further throug
 h the Raven Players’ ScripTease program. It is the story of a young Chic
 ano from Chicago\, lured to the East Coast by an Ivy League scholarship. A
 s he tries to make a life there\, he neglects family relationships and dee
 p cultural roots established throughout generations. It takes his mother
 ’s nearly fatal heart attack\, help from a Jewish therapist\, and the vi
 sitation of the spirits of his long dead relatives (and of his historical 
 idol\, Pancho Villa) to help him realize what he’s lost\, and how to get
  it back. Dancing spirits\, who are intertwined throughout the play\, help
  remind “Chicano” of the joy in dancing\, especially when dancing is m
 uch more than dancing.\n\nBy John and Gabriel Fraire\n\nDirected by Jenna 
 Vera Dolcini\n\n**August 7\, 8\, 9\, \\*13\, 14\, 15\, 16**\n\n**Friday an
 d Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Matinee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value 
 Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission: Adults:** $25\n\n**Student w/ID:** $1
 0\n\n**\\*Value Thursday Performance:** Pay What You Can
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/who-will-dance-with-pancho-villa-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A SALSA MUSICALITY AND BODY MOVEMENT WORKSHOP
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T150000
UID:260706RBSoYGEyaEKYIYospe9USQ
DESCRIPTION:DATE: August 15\n\nTIME: 1:30 pm – 3:00 pm\n\nWHERE: Salsa D
 ance Marin\, 4140 Redwood hwy 8\, San Rafael\n\nUnlock the body isolation 
 and salsa musicality. We are going to demystify the complex rhythms of the
  Salsa orchestra\, unlock the fluid mechanics of authentic Latin body isol
 ation\, and teach you how to actually feel the music. Whether you want to 
 dance with more confidence\, find your unique flavor\, or simply connect d
 eeper to the rhythm\, you are in the right place.\n\n“We dance because o
 f the music”- let’s discover what that really means!\n\nA three part w
 orkshop:\n\nBody Movement and Isolation Workout\n\nStarting from the head 
 and working all the way to the feet\, we’ll explore body isolations and 
 learn how to combine them into movement that feels natural\, expressive an
 d uniquely yours! This full body warm- up increases mobility\, builds stre
 ngth and prepares you to move with greater confidence.\n\nMUSICALITY\n\nWe
 ’ll listen to and dance with different Afro-Cuban rhythms-including sals
 a\, rumba\, son and cha cha to develop a deeper understanding of musical s
 tructure. Learn to recognize rhythm\, phrasing and instrumentation so you 
 can respond naturally to the music and develop your own style.\n\nPutting 
 It All Together!\n\nWe’ll apply everything you’ve learned through fund
 amental footwork\, rhythm exercises and add in partner concepts. Whether y
 ou dance “On 1”\, “On 2”\, Cuban Casino\, Rueda or simply love mov
 ing your body to great music\, you’ll discover new ways to listen\, inte
 rpret and express what you hear…and experience dance in a whole new way\
 n\nAbout your Instructor- Jennifer Lehr\n\nDance has been my creative outl
 et for as long as I can remember. Since discovering Latin Dance in 2010\, 
 I’ve developed a deep appreciation for the connection between music\, mo
 vement\, and emotional expression.\n\nJoin me as we explore movement\, mus
 icality\, and timing while building confidence\, improving technique\, and
  celebrating the joy of dance.\n\nCome Ready to Move\, Listen and be Inspi
 red!
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/a-salsa-musicality-and-body-movement-works
 hop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Caesar - Shakespeare in the Park(ing Lot)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T211500
UID:260703WfgD7cJB40GLgP-_iR2hOg
DESCRIPTION:Free Shakespeare in the Park(ing Lot). Elections\, ego\, fear.
  Caesar climbs. The republic fractures.\n\nWe are excited to announce ‘S
 hakespeare in the Park(ing Lot)’ 2026.\n\n***Free Shakespeare.***\n\n**C
 aesar**\n\nPresented by the Jacobethan Theatre Workshop.\n\nDoors open at
  6.75pm\, performance at 7.30pm.\n\nOn Sundays\, doors open at 2.15pm with
  as 3pm start.\n\nDirected by Lukas Raphael\n\n*Caesar* unfolds in 100 mi
 nutes of sharp\, modern storytelling. A political system strains under amb
 ition\, loyalty fractures\, and public rhetoric turns volatile. With minim
 al staging and contemporary dress\, the play lands uncomfortably close to 
 the present: a study of power\, perception\, and how quickly a republic ca
 n shift.\n\nNo intermission.\n\nA local selection of wine and beer can be 
 purchased in the theater.
LOCATION:Life On Art
URL:https://www.jacobethan.org/parking-lot
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
