BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coming Home to Yourself A Self-Compassion Series with Horses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T193000
UID:260713ARp8N-qJ0U28z6WAft_SLg
DESCRIPTION:Coming Home to Yourself\n\nA Self-Compassion Series with Horse
 s\n\nThursday Evenings Open House: July 9\, 2026Series: July 16 – August
  27\, 2026\n\nNo Session on July 30th\n\nTime: 6-7:30pm\n\nComing Home to 
 Yourself  will be held at the Private Vacation Pasture of Heart & Mind E
 quine\, located on the border of Marin and Sonoma Counties\, along the 101
  freeway corridor\, close to the EarthRise Center at 101 San Antonio Road.
  Directions sent after registration.\n\nCome explore our self-compassion s
 eries with horses\n\nIn this series participants will interact with the ho
 rses to build trust\, establish boundaries\, and mirror the animals' prese
 nt-moment awareness\, helping to heal trauma\, reduce anxiety\, and improv
 e self-care.\n\nYour Registration Includes:\n\n- Six guided equine-assiste
 d self-compassion experiences\n\n- Facilitated group discussions and refle
 ction\n\n- Hands-on interactions with the horses\n\n- Workbook and between
 -session practices\n\n- Sound healing and breathwork exercises\n\n- Journa
 ling and creative expression activities\n\n- A supportive community of fel
 low participants\n\n- Ongoing opportunities to deepen self-awareness\, sel
 f-trust\, and self-care\n\nNo horse experience required\n\nLearn more abou
 t Heart & Mind Equine here: https://www.heartmindequine.com/
LOCATION:Heart and Mind Equine
URL:https://www.alanefreund.com/self-compassion-with-horses/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T193000
UID:260415fRUuHIT7_kioA-AnS-VApQ
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Erica Sunshine Lee
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T000000
UID:260327P4kL3Lsd0UeVRYT-SWT8hg
DESCRIPTION:Bay Area's favorite "Georgia Gypsy" returns back to the city w
 here this Georgia native started her band in 2007.  Now Erica Sunshine Lee
  is a country singer-songwriter and International Touring Artist\, Nashvil
 le Recording artist with 11 original albums with her traditional roots and
  tropical flair\, often infusing her authentical country music with island
  vibes and coastal rhythms. She's had over 66 songs recorded by other Nash
 ville and International Recording artists. Known for her captivating alto 
 and raspy southern voice and dynamic raw songwriting\, Erica seamlessly fu
 ses the storytelling of country music with the relaxed\, feel-good atmosph
 ere of tropical rock. Her songs celebrate everything from love and heartbr
 eak to adventure and freedom\, all while reflecting her sunny\, genuine pe
 rsonality and easy-going\, yet adventurous and bold lifestyle.\n\nA Nashvi
 lle-based and Georgia native artist with deep Southern roots\, this phenom
 enal songbird has also earned recognition at the Tropical Rock Music Award
 s for her ability to merge country storytelling with island-inspired sound
 s\, winning 5 time TRMA female artist of the year. Playing at world renown
 ed festivals: Summerfest\, Cheyenne Frontier Days\, Fiji Jazz & Blues Fest
 \, New Zealand Jazz & Blues Fest\, Summer Chill\, Meeting of the Minds\, K
 ey West Songwriter's Festival\, Millbrae Art & Wine Fest\, South by Southw
 est\, CMA week Nashville\, Tin Pan South\, Tamworth Country Music Festival
  \\(Australia\\)\, Voghera Country Music Fest \\(Italy\\)\, fairs and fest
 ivals across the USA and more\, her catchy tunes and infectious energy hav
 e garnered a devoted and loyal following! Her music is known for its infec
 tious hooks\, laid-back groove\, and evocative lyrics\, and she brings suc
 h a dynamic world class stage presence with her witty humor and larger tha
 n life personality. Whether she’s singing about a beachside romance or a
  life full of ups and downs\, addiction\, heartache\, miscarriage\, murder
 \, and redemption\, Erica Sunshine Lee’s music knows no boundary and is 
 a celebration of life's joys and challenges\, with a splash of lime\, suns
 hine and a breeze of reality\, Jesus and island vibes.  Erica Sunshine Lee
  is a children's author\, founder and advocate of the Key West Chick Fest\
 , empowering and encouraging female entrepreneurs and songwriters\, and an
  inspirational International touring artist inspiring people everywhere of
  all ages\, genres and races to follow their dreams and change the world f
 or the better!
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108104161?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
